  "result": "The bug was in `findIssueById` in `src/server/repositories/issue-repository.ts` — it accepted an `orgId` parameter but never used it in the SQL `WHERE` clause, only filtering by `issues.id`. That meant `getIssue()` (called from the issue detail page, the `[issueId]` API route, and `archive-issue.ts`) would happily return any issue by ID regardless of which org it belonged to, even though the actor's membership check (`assertOrgScope`) was against the requester's own org. Sibling function `findIssueByNumber` already scoped correctly via `orgPredicate(issues.orgId, orgId)`.\n\nFixed by adding the same `orgPredicate(issues.orgId, orgId)` filter to `findIssueById`'s query, so cross-org issue IDs now resolve to \"not found\" instead of leaking the other tenant's issue.",
